SUMMARY:2 Hr Spirited Improv Community Playshop
DESCRIPTION:Awakening Asheville\nABOUT SPIRITED IMPROV\n\n**Spirited Impro
 v is a heart-centered community experience that uses improvisational play 
 as the container for spiritual growth\, personal transformation\, and auth
 entic connection.** Rather than focusing on comedy or performance\, we use
  improv as a living practice\, one that invites presence\, trust\, curiosi
 ty\, and responsiveness in the moment.\n\nFacilitated by Jessica Chilton\,
  who brings over 20 years of improvisational performing arts experience an
 d 16 years as an expressive arts therapist\, weaving creativity\, spiritua
 lity\, and presence into a safe\, transformative group experience.\n\nWHAT
  IS THE COMMUNITY PLAYSHOP ALL ABOUT?\n\nCome see what Spirited Improv is 
 all about. No commitment required. No experience necessary. On the final d
 ay of our current multi-week series\, we open our doors to newcomers\, fri
 ends\, and anyone whose curiosity has been quietly calling them.\n\nThis i
 s a rare chance to step inside the experience and feel it for yourself: sa
 cred play\, authentic connection\, and collective joy with a group that ha
 s been building something real together.\n\nWhether you settle in as a wit
 ness or decide to leap into the play\, you'll leave with a felt sense of w
 hat Spirited Improv truly is - and what becomes possible when a community 
 gathers in radical acceptance and love.\n\nWHAT PAST PARTICIPANTS ARE SAYI
 NG\n\n“Spirited Improv is authentic\, vulnerable and connective. It meet
 s my need to deeply feel\, be seen and see others. On my first night I exp
 erienced such a profound healing experience after sharing what was on my h
 eart. It was like a sound\, healing touch\, full moon energy bath that ope
 ned my heart. ” \\~ Kate\n\n“Spirited Improv is a fun and little bit e
 dgy way of interacting with the mystery of the moment. You decide how much
  you want to interact or observe from the audience so you never have to do
  anything you don't want to do. It is an opportunity to let go of control 
 and explore the spontaneity of life and creativity in a supportive\, safe 
 environment..” \\~ Kenyon\n\n“I got to play\, move my body\, laugh\, t
 ake joy in watching my friends come alive\, give and receive big hugs\, an
 d feel the presence of the ancestors who always join me. There’s somethi
 ng so sacred about being present with others while we play\, witness and e
 mbody what is.” \\~ Sue\n\nMORE INFO\nPAY WHAT YOU WANT $1 - $50\n\nhttp
 s://SpiritedImprov.com
